[0.640, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[2D\u001b[3B\r\u001b[4A  So \"needs it back on verify\" means: the counter isn't fire-and-forget. It's a small piece of per-credential state that\r\u001b[1B   round-trips\u001b[1Cthrough\u001b[1Cyour\u001b[1CDB\u001b[1Con\u001b[1Cevery\u001b[1Clogin\u001b[1C—\u001b[1Cread\u001b[1Cit\u001b[1Cin,\u001b[1Chand\u001b[1Cit\u001b[1Cto\u001b[1Cthe\u001b[1Clibrary,\u001b[1Cwrite\u001b[1Cthe\u001b[1Cnew\u001b[1Cvalue\u001b[1Cout.\u001b[1CSame\u001b[1Cstory\r\u001b[1B  for \u001b[38;2;87;105;247mpublicKey\u001b[39m and \u001b[38;2;87;105;247mcredential_id\u001b[39m: those are also DB → library inputs on every verify. The counter just happens to be   \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bthe one that\u001b[1Calso\u001b[1Cgets\u001b[1Cwritten\u001b[1Cback.\u001b[59C                     \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m❯ \u001b[39m\u001b[7m \u001b[27m\r\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[2C\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m--\u001b[1CINSERT\u001b[1C--\u001b[83CNow\u001b[1Cusing\u001b[1Cextra\u001b[1Cusage\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[2C\u001b[3A\u001b[?2026l"]
