[0.003, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[72D\u001b[3B\r\u001b[7A\u001b[48;2;240;240;240m\u001b[38;2;175;175;175m❯ \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mOK. So personally I have this thing happen with passkeys where sometimes it tries to go through Bitwarden (I use a \u001b[39m   \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mbrowser plugin, which is why I was fixated on that), and sometimes it just prompts for my Yubikey. I have some \u001b[39m       \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mpasskeys in BW and some through my yubikey. Is it the stored transports on the server that are hinting that? \u001b[39m         \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mSometimes I find it annoying that I am routed through several dialoggs\u001b[39m                                                \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m         \u001b[1C \u001b[1C    \u001b[1C  \u001b[1C        \u001b[1C    \u001b[1C \u001b[1C  \u001b[1C      \u001b[1C       \u001b[1C       \u001b[1C         \r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m✳\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;215;119;87mFlummoxing… \u001b[39m                                                                                                          \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B            \r\r\n\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m───────────────────"]
