[0.311, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[2D\u001b[3B\r\u001b[4A  For a receipt scanner demo, that's probably fine. For anything with value to the user, most designers add at least one\r\u001b[1B   escape\u001b[1Chatch:\u001b[1Can\u001b[1Cemail\u001b[1Cfor\u001b[1Crecovery,\u001b[1Cor\u001b[1Ca\u001b[1C\"save\u001b[1Cthis\u001b[1Crecovery\u001b[1Ccode\u001b[1Csomewhere\"\u001b[1Cflow\u001b[1Cat\u001b[1Csignup.\u001b[1CNeither\u001b[1Cis\u001b[1Crequired\u001b[1Cby\r\u001b[1B  the protocol, but both are common concessions.                                                                        \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B            \r\r\n\u001b[2C\u001b[1mSummary\u001b[22m\r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m❯ \u001b[39m\u001b[7m \u001b[27m\r\r\n\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m──────────────────────────"]
