[0.514, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[2D\u001b[3B\r\u001b[4A  \u001b[1mStrict\u001b[22m is tighter — even a link-click from outside doesn't carry the cookie. The downside is that users who click a   \r\u001b[1B  link\u001b[1Cfrom\u001b[1Cemail,\u001b[1CSlack,\u001b[1CGoogle\u001b[1Csearch,\u001b[1Cetc.\u001b[1Carrive\u001b[1Clogged-out,\u001b[1Chave\u001b[1Cto\u001b[1Clog\u001b[1Cin\u001b[1Cagain,\u001b[1Cand\u001b[1C\u001b[3mthen\u001b[1C\u001b[23mland\u001b[1Con\u001b[1Cthe\u001b[1Cpage\u001b[1Cthey\r\u001b[1B  wanted. For apps where that re-auth hop is fine (banking, high-value dashboards), Strict is arguably correct. For most\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B apps it's overzealous.\r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m❯ \u001b[39m\u001b[7m \u001b[27m\r\r\n\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m───────────────────────"]
[0.000, "o", "─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[2C\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m--\u001b[1CINSERT\u001b[1C--\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[2C\u001b[3A\u001b[?2026l"]
