[0.309, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[2D\u001b[3B\r\u001b[4A  Exactly this distinction. A pre-auth session has \u001b[38;2;87;105;247mreq.session\u001b[39m populated but \u001b[38;2;87;105;247mreq.user\u001b[39m unset, and that's the correct     \r\u001b[1B  state\u001b[1Cfor\u001b[1C\u001b[38;2;87;105;247m/api/auth/register/options\u001b[1C\u001b[39mto\u001b[1Cuse\u001b[1C—\u001b[1Cit\u001b[1Cneeds\u001b[1Cthe\u001b[1Csession\u001b[1C(to\u001b[1Cstore\u001b[1Cthe\u001b[1Cchallenge)\u001b[1Cbut\u001b[1Cmustn't\u001b[1Ctreat\u001b[1Cthe\r\u001b[1B  caller as authenticated. Routes that operate on user data guard on \u001b[38;2;87;105;247mreq.user\u001b[39m, which is only set after a successful     \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bverify. The two-slot\u001b[1Cdesign\u001b[1Cmakes\u001b[1Cthe\u001b[1C\"halfway\"\u001b[1Cstate\u001b[1Cexpressible\u001b[1Cwithout\u001b[1Cbolts-on.\r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m·\u001b[1CIdeating…\u001b[1C\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m(35s\u001b[1C·\u001b[1C↓\u001b[1C875\u001b[1Ctokens)\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m \u001b[1C⎿\u001b[1C Tip:\u001b[1CUse\u001b[1C/btw\u001b[1Cto\u001b[1Cask\u001b[1Ca\u001b[1Cquick\u001b[1Cside\u001b[1Cquestion\u001b[1Cwithout\u001b[1Cinterrupting\u001b[1CClaude's\u001b[1Ccurrent\u001b[1Cwork\u001b[39m\r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m───────────────────────────"]
