[0.961, "o", "\u001b]0;⠐ Implement passkey authentication system\u0007"]
[0.190, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[2D\u001b[3B\r\u001b[4A  The real tradeoff you're identifying is: \u001b[1mthe DB models the storage, not the protocol.\u001b[22m The ceremony has phases         \r\u001b[1B  (challenge\u001b[1Cissued\u001b[1C→\u001b[1Cchallenge\u001b[1Cconsumed\u001b[1C→\u001b[1Cuser\u001b[1Cbound),\u001b[1Cbut\u001b[1Cthe\u001b[1CDB\u001b[1Conly\u001b[1Ccaptures\u001b[1Cthe\u001b[1C\u001b[3mresult\u001b[1C\u001b[23mof\u001b[1Ceach\u001b[1Cphase,\u001b[1Cnot\u001b[1Cthe\r\u001b[1B  transition itself. That's by design — the DB is not the state machine, the handler code is. If you wanted the DB to \u001b[3mbe\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[23m the state machine,\u001b[1Cyou'd\u001b[1Cdo\u001b[1C#2\u001b[1C(explicit\u001b[1Cstate\u001b[1Ccolumn\u001b[1Cwith\u001b[1CCHECK)\u001b[1Cor\u001b[1C#1\u001b[1C(tables\u001b[1Cas\u001b[1Cstates).\r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[38;2;102;102;1"]
[0.000, "o", "02m❯ \u001b[39m\u001b[7m \u001b[27m\r\r\n\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[2C\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m--\u001b[1CINSERT\u001b[1C--\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[2C\u001b[3A\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.507, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[2D\u001b[3B\r\u001b[4A  \u001b[1mWhat I'd actually recommend for this app\u001b[22m                                                                              \r\u001b[1B   \r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m❯ \u001b[39m\u001b[7m \u001b[27m           \r\r\n\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[2C\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m--\u001b[1CINSERT\u001b[1C--\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[2C\u001b[3A\u001b[?2026l"]
